<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kodama Gentarō</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1852">1852</a>–<a href="/years/1906">1906</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Kodama Gentaro</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kodama Gentarō (1852–1906) was a Japanese general and statesman. As Governor-General of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taiwan">Taiwan</a> from 1898 to 1906, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/goto-shinpei">Gotō Shinpei</a> as his civil administrator, he consolidated colonial control and promoted the island's economic development. He also served as army minister and home minister, and as chief of staff of the Manchurian Army he directed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>'s campaigns in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russo-japanese-war">Russo-Japanese War</a> of 1904–1905.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kodama-gentaro.jpg" alt="Kodama Gentarō" width="320" height="421" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kodama_Gentar%C5%8D.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
